  "name": "ANTI RNP ANTIBODY",
  "code": "2677",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Antibodies to U1 small nuclear ribonucleoprotein particle (snRNP) are associated with various Connective Tissue Diseases&nbsp;(CTD). The most common occurrence is in patients with several rheumatic diseases including systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)&nbsp;and mixed connective tissue disease (MCTD).</p>\n<p><strong>CLINICAL SIGNIFICANCE</strong></p>\n<p><br>Anti RNP Antibody is considered as diagnostic marker of mixed connective tissue disease (MCTD). Used in this indication the antibodies&nbsp;achieve a sensitivity of ~99% and a specificity of ~99%% in absence of both anti Sm and anti-dsDNA antibodies.</p>\n<p><br><strong>LIMITATIONS:</strong></p>\n<p><br>-A positive result must be used in association with clinical evaluation and diagnostic procedure.<br>-Samples from apparent blood donor may contain autoantibodies.<br>-If the sample contains elevated levels of immune complexes or other immunoglobulin aggregates, results may sometime be false&nbsp;positive.&nbsp;</p>",
